\details{
Provides methods for retrieving market data from Binance's USD-M Futures API,
including exchange info, klines, mark prices, funding rates, tickers,
order books, open interest, and trade history.

Inherits from \link{BinanceBase}. All methods support both synchronous and
asynchronous execution depending on the \code{async} parameter at construction.
\subsection{Purpose and Scope}{
\itemize{
\item \strong{Exchange Info}: Retrieve futures trading pair metadata including precision, filters, and contract type.
\item \strong{Klines}: Fetch historical candlestick data for futures contracts.
\item \strong{Mark Price}: Access mark prices and funding rate information.
\item \strong{Funding Rates}: Get historical funding rate data.
\item \strong{Tickers}: Access real-time price data for individual symbols or all pairs.
\item \strong{Order Books}: Get order book depth snapshots.
\item \strong{Open Interest}: Retrieve open interest data for futures contracts.
\item \strong{Trade History}: Retrieve recent trades for any symbol.
\item \strong{Index/Mark Price Klines}: Fetch historical index price and mark price candlestick data.
}
}

\subsection{Usage}{

All methods are public endpoints requiring no authentication.
The base URL defaults to \verb{https://fapi.binance.com} via \code{\link[=get_futures_base_url]{get_futures_base_url()}}.
}

\subsection{Official Documentation}{

\href{https://binance-docs.github.io/apidocs/futures/en/#market-data-endpoints}{Binance USD-M Futures Market Data}
}

